{"name":"Kitten’s Paw","hex":"#daa89b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kitten","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat, especially before sexual maturity (reached at about seven months).","A young rabbit, rat, hedgehog, squirrel, fox, beaver, badger, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give birth to kittens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitten"},{"term":"paw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Pawnee."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft foot of a mammal or other animal, generally a quadruped, that has claws or nails; comparable to a human hand or foot.","A hand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plicatula gibbosa","blocks":[{"text":"Plicatula gibbosa, commonly known as the Atlantic kitten's paw, is a species of bivalve mollusc in the family Plicatulidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Plicatula_gibbosa_%28MNHN-IM-2000-33995%29_002.jpeg/330px-Plicatula_gibbosa_%28MNHN-IM-2000-33995%29_002.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plicatula_gibbosa","wikidata":"Q3017840"},{"title":"Paw","blocks":[{"text":"A paw is the soft foot-like part of a mammal, generally a quadruped, that has claws. To paw is for an animal to use their paws, usually gently or for digging, or for a human to use their hands in the manner of an animal's paw."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Paw_and_pads.jpg/330px-Paw_and_pads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paw","wikidata":"Q219588"},{"title":"Kitten","blocks":[{"text":"A kitten is a juvenile cat. After being born, kittens display primary altriciality and are fully dependent on their mothers for survival. They normally do not open their eyes for seven to ten days. After 